## Cross-stack test placement

Apply only the rows for stack roots that exist in the selected composition.

| Asset | Location | Naming |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Frontend unit | {{testing.frontendUnitRoot}} | *{{testing.unitSuffix}} |
| Frontend integration | {{testing.frontendIntegrationRoot}} | *{{testing.integrationSuffix}} |
| Backend unit/spec | {{testing.backendUnitRoot}} | *{{testing.unitSuffix}} |
| Backend migration | {{testing.backendMigrationRoot}} | *{{testing.unitSuffix}} |
| Backend integration | {{testing.backendIntegrationRoot}} | *{{testing.integrationSuffix}} |
| End-to-end | {{testing.e2eRoot}} | *{{testing.e2eSuffix}} |
| Fixtures | {{testing.fixtureRoot}} | descriptive, stable input names |
| Generated test assets | {{testing.generatedAssetRoot}} | generator-defined deterministic names |

Unit tests may be colocated with source: {{testing.colocated}}. Colocated
frontend and backend specs may sit beside a source file or in a feature-owned
tests directory beneath an application root. Centralized migration specs use
the configured migration root; application-local migration specs may remain in
an application-owned `src/db/tests/migrations` boundary.

Fixtures are maintained inputs and must not be mixed with generated output.
Generated assets must be reproducible and must not be edited as source. A
separate framework capability owns runner selection, discovery configuration,
and test execution commands.
